# Language parity

Same public workflow in C#, Rust, and TypeScript. Do not add a helper, extra call, or auto-path in one language only.

`Defaults` / `Create` / `Register` mean the same thing everywhere. If env already has `INSTALLED_PROVIDERS` and `DATABASE_URL`, `Create` / `create` / `create_default` applies those defaults and registers the listed factories. Do not require `install`, `register_from`, or a hand-built defaults dictionary in one language when the others do not.

```csharp
var ds = DatasourceFactory.Create();
```

```rust
let ds = create_default()?;
```

```typescript
const ds = Datasource.create();
```
